  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_007 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.542), and RNA signal dominates (rna_only scgpt=0.530 vs image_only=0.33). However, all completed experiments use scgpt as the RNA encoder; scvi_n200 and pca_n2000 remain untested in the multimodal setting. Uncertainty: We do not know whether scgpt's learned representation is specifically required or whether another learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) performs comparably with the same image/fusion/aggregation stack. This experiment (config_019: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) changes only the RNA encoder relative to config_007, giving a clean single-variable comparison. If scvi_n200 matches scgpt, the RNA representation family is flexible and we can focus budget on image/fusion/profile choices; if it falls well short, scgpt is confirmed as the critical RNA encoder and further RNA-encoder exploration is deprioritized. This is the highest-information next step because the RNA encoder is the largest untested design axis and the dominant performance driver."
}

